{
  "version": 1,
  "bespokeIdentifier": "cosmo-automations",
  "title": "Recover failed payments overnight",
  "instructions": [
    "Every night, billing needs the failed payments from the last 24 hours dealt with \u2014 and how they are dealt with depends on who the customer is.",
    "Build a workflow that:",
    "1. Runs on a schedule, and reads the failed payments with the query `SELECT invoice, accountId, amount, reason, attempts FROM payments WHERE status = 'failed'` using the Billing DB credential.",
    "2. The query joins two tables, so some invoices come back twice. Each invoice must appear once.",
    "3. Loads the `Accounts` table from Airtable base `appBilling`. Each record has an `accountId`, a `company`, a `tier` and a `manager` email.",
    "4. Attaches each payment's account to it, matching on `accountId`.",
    "5. Routes payments by `tier`: `enterprise`, `mid_market` and `self_serve` each go their own way, and any other tier must be flagged rather than dropped.",
    "6. enterprise: the three largest by `amount` get a personal email to the account manager, and a row appended to the `Outreach` sheet in document `sheetRecovery2026`.",
    "7. mid_market: retry the charge two invoices at a time by POSTing to `https://billing.acme.test/v1/invoices/{invoice}/retry`, then tag the payments as retried.",
    "8. self_serve: tag the payments for dunning and create a record in the `DunningQueue` Airtable table.",
    "9. Any other tier: post an alert to Slack on `#billing-alerts`.",
    "10. Finally, bring the escalated, retried and dunning payments back together and post one summary to `#billing-ops` reading exactly `Recovery run: 9 payments handled, 28558 EUR still at risk`."
  ],
  "palette": {
    "include": [
      "scheduleTrigger",
      "manualTrigger",
      "webhook",
      "postgres",
      "airtable",
      "googleSheets",
      "gmail",
      "slack",
      "httpRequest",
      "removeDuplicates",
      "merge",
      "switch",
      "sort",
      "limit",
      "loopOverItems",
      "set",
      "filter",
      "if",
      "splitOut",
      "aggregate",
      "noOp"
    ],
    "exclude": [],
    "excludeNote": "Code is deliberately not offered. The assertions check that the routing, the join and the de-duplication were done with the nodes that name them, so a Code node producing the right rows would be rejected for the wrong reason. See the README authoring guide on mechanism vs outcome."
  },
